`A(x,y)=(γx+(δ-γ)y, δy)`,

with `P∘A=γ^8 δ^3 P` and Jacobian factor `γ^{-119}δ^{-44}`. After `J=1`, one parameter remains; it acts by `β ↦ β/(γ^3 δ)`. Solving `γ^{13}=β^{44}` over algebraically closed `k` sets `β=1` (hence the `e^{12}` coefficient to 1) jointly with every other row family. The local stretch `Qc_{r,q}→α^q Qc_{r,q}` still does **not** preserve `y=0`; it is not the joint-ideal group element.

